# Quiz System: Student App (Android)

- LAN-only. Must work with NO internet. No cloud services or online APIs.
- Stack: Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, OkHttp WebSocket, NsdManager for discovery, CameraX + the bundled ML Kit barcode scanner (com.google.mlkit:barcode-scanning, NOT the Play-services version that may download a model). Don't swap the stack.
- docs/protocol.md is the source of truth for messages and discovery. Never invent or change message types. If something is unclear or missing, stop and ask.
- The server is authoritative. The phone never scores answers or keeps authoritative time.
- The server uses ws:// (not wss://), so allow cleartext traffic to LAN addresses via a network security config.
- Build only the current step. No extra features.
- Keep code in small packages: net/, data/, ui/.
- During a running quiz never use window-based UI (Dialog, AlertDialog, DropdownMenu, Popup, ModalBottomSheet). They steal window focus and cause a pause. Use in-composition UI only.
